<title>UK: Black Sea, Baltic oil exports down 388k bpd on week.</title>
<headline>Black Sea, Baltic oil exports down 388k bpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 388,000 barrels a day (bpd) to 1.451 million bpd in the second week of January but were little changed compared to the same week last year, consultancy Petro-Logistics said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from the former Soviet Baltic and Black Sea ports fell 187,000 bpd on the week to 992,000 bpd.</p>
<p>Fuel exports were down 143,000 on the week at 168,000 bpd but were 32,000 bpd higher than last year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports were down 169,000 at 122,000 bpd and 272,000 bpd lower than last year.</p>
<p>Gasoline and jet exports combined were up 111,000 at 169,130 bpd and included 78,000 bpd from Romania/Bulgaria.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the first week of January.</p>
<p>		   Crude	 Fuel	Gas Oil   Mogas/Jet  Total</p>
<p>FSU		952,517     181,635   114,403   64,561    1,313,116</p>
<p>Romania/</p>
